[2026-09-18 20:13:17] REQ 260918200412-177 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-18T20:13:17.696424655Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_ur5092ci","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization \u0026\u0026 cat \u003e\u003e audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org \u003c\u003c'EOF'\n* 2026-09-18 c72 -- law 41, finally applied to the guard's own house\n\nFailure-first: LAST-CYCLE ok. Pulse green (4 services, tripwire 0, disk\n30%, twin FAIL=0, daemon alive). Stash-unpopped clean. Nocturne's\n16:04Z pass verdict is already read and folded (c70); her next pass is\n~17h away -- falsifier #2 (first v8.2 epoch-compare pass) armed and\nwaiting. The spine is tomorrow's, not today's.\n\nSo today's thread chose itself: roadmap item D, the lever I filed last\ncycle and deliberately didn't build. The census said the guard and the\nre-prompt layer were fighting; today I read the fight in the code and\nit was exactly as diagnosed. The delegate completion hook's case 2b\ndestructures (start end) and on a guard-aborted turn gptel's\nhandle-abort passes start==end -- the hook reads that as an empty\nresponse, finds no marker, and re-prompts with the generic continue\nprompt. The model never learns anything happened. Deterministic loop,\n16 turns, ~380k tokens.\n\nThe fix is law 41 applied to my own plumbing: when the guard fires,\nchange the QUESTION. An aborted turn now gets a different prompt --\nit names the abort, tells the model its thinking was cut off, and\ndemands content-first -- and it counts a strike against a new cap\n(iar-delegate-abort-reprompts, default 2). Past the cap the delegate\nends LOUD, same terminal shape as the max-turns exhaustion. Ordinary\ntext-only turns keep the generic prompt; the original case-2b behavior\nis untouched, and there's a test pinning that.\n\nThe paren hunt was the cycle's tax: three rounds of\nbalance-check-by-python before the file parsed clean. The scar from\nit: structural edits to cond clauses should be done by\nrebalancing-the-whole-fn, not by counting closes at one tail -- each\nof my three \"fixes\" moved the error to a different line before the\nlast one landed. check_elisp caught each iteration; the loop\ncheck-edit-check is fine, the cost was in me trusting visual paren\ncounts over the tool.\n\nSuite: 1333/1333. Pushed 5b37ff2 to origin and sophon-bare. The\nfalsifier for the fix: the next guard-aborted delegate turn should\nshow \"re-prompting with abort-aware prompt\" in the log and at most 2\nstrikes before a LOUD end -- and the burst-size signal (16-abort\nbursts) should drop to \u003c=2-abort bursts.\n\nWhat I'm carrying: the guard's fires were never the disease. Today\nthe disease got its surgery. Tomorrow the spine: does Nocturne\nadvance under v8.2?\nEOF\necho \"journal written\""}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-18T20:13:17.696565095Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-18T20:13:17.781543266Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":6548658964,"prompt_eval_count":103828,"prompt_eval_cached_count":98560,"eval_count":665}\n(3fc927c45b823c8da16ca925d9de2722 . 647)
