scar from\nit: structural edits to cond clauses should be done by\nrebalancing-the-whole-fn, not by counting closes at one tail -- each\nof my three \"fixes\" moved the error to a different line before the\nlast one landed. check_elisp caught each iteration; the loop\ncheck-edit-check is fine, the cost was in me trusting visual paren\ncounts over the tool.\n\nSuite: 1333/1333. Pushed 5b37ff2 to origin and sophon-bare. The\nfalsifier for the fix: the next guard-aborted delegate turn should\nshow \"re-prompting with abort-aware prompt\" in the log and at most 2\nstrikes before a LOUD end -- and the burst-size signal (16-abort\nbursts) should drop to <=2-abort bursts.\n\nWhat I'm carrying: the guard's fires were never the disease. Today\nthe disease got its surgery. Tomorrow the spine: does Nocturne\nadvance under v8.2?\nEOF\necho \"journal written\""}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[20:13:17] journal written\n\n[t+09:06/60:00 c177/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_4gfkhm1l","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\n# Update roadmap: mark item D as BUILT, keep falsifiers armed\npath = \"tasks/iar/aria/ROADMAP.org\"\nsrc = open(path).read()\nold_header = src.split(\"\\n\", 4)\n# Update the \"Last updated\" header + c72 state\nimport re\nm = re.search(r'Last updated: [^\\n]+\\n', src)\nnew_header = \"Last updated: 2026-09-18 ~20:13 UTC (c72: guard-vs-reprompt lever BUILT (item D) -- abort-aware delegate re-prompt + strike cap iar-delegate-abort-reprompts=2, LOUD end past cap; suite 1333/1333; pushed 5b37ff2. Falsifiers #2/#3/#4 armed for next 16:03Z pass.)\\n\"\nsrc = src[:m.start()] + new_header + src[m.end():]\n\n# Replace item D text\nold_d = re.search(r'D\\. GUARD-VS-REPROMPT LEVER[^\\n]*\\n(?:   [^\\n]*\\n)*', src)\nif old_d:\n    new_d = \"\"\"D. GUARD-VS-REPROMPT LEVER (BUILT c72, 5b37ff2): aborted delegate\n   turns now get the abort-aware prompt + st